{"records":[{"id":"66kbk28dzh","title":"Ph+ALL and P2RX1","description":"raw data of P2RX1 promotes mitochondrial apoptosis via calcium/CaM KII-mediated suppression of PI3K/Akt signaling in Philadelphia chromosome-positive acute lymphoblastic leukemia","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-12-05T00:23:18.073Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66kbk28dzh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66kbk28dzh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"xiao bing","last_name":"li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Design"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xr3pd87gpd","title":"Ph+ALL and Luteolin","description":"raw data of Luteolin induces apoptosis in Philadelphia chromosome-positive acute lymphoblastic leukemia cell by regulating the PI3K/AKT signaling pathway\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-27T10:07:19.815Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xr3pd87gpd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xr3pd87gpd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"qin","last_name":"ren","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Network Pharmacology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"rzcvr5vvh9","title":"Data for: Anterior segment infiltration of acute lymphoblastic leukemia: case report and systematic review  ","description":"Search terms used in systematic review component of manuscript entitled \"Anterior segment infiltration of acute lymphoblastic leukemia: case report and systematic review\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-04-23T09:44:03.303Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/rzcvr5vvh9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/rzcvr5vvh9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ashley","last_name":"Yu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ruth","last_name":"Padmore","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michael D.","last_name":"O'Connor","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Stephanie C.","last_name":"Chan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yiannis","last_name":"Iordanous","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Ophthalmology"],"journal_issn":["00084182"]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fz7d6x4bwx","title":"Artificial Intelligence Reveals the Predictions of Hematological Indexes in Children with Acute Leukemia","description":"Childhood leukemia is a prevalent form of pediatric cancer, with acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) and acute myeloid leukemia (AML) being the primary manifestations. Timely treatment has significantly enhanced survival rates for children with acute leukemia. This study aimed to develop an early and comprehensive predictor for hematologic malignancies in children by examining nutritional markers, key leukemia indicators, and granulocytes in patients' blood. Using a machine learning algorithm and ten indices, 826 pediatric patients with ALL and 255 children with AML were analyzed, comparing them with a control group of 200 healthy children. The study revealed notable differences, including higher indicators in boys compared to girls and significant variations in most biochemical indicators between leukemia patients and healthy children. Employing a random forest model resulted in an Area Under the Curve (AUC) of 0.950 for predicting leukemia subtypes and an AUC of 0.909 for forecasting AML. This research introduces an efficient diagnostic tool for early screening of childhood blood cancers and underscores the potential of artificial intelligence in modern healthcare.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-02-11T03:29:59.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fz7d6x4bwx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fz7d6x4bwx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Haiyang","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Coding in Methodology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xz4m36dgzh","title":"B-ALL blood, marrow, and CSF compound abundance data","description":"Unscaled compound abundance data from untargeted metabolomics assays performed in blood plasma, bone marrow aspirate, and cerebrospinal fluid from N=10 children with B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia at the end of induction chemotherapy.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-09-22T19:53:38.561Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xz4m36dgzh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xz4m36dgzh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jeremy","last_name":"Schraw","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Metabolomics","Acute B-Cell Lymphoblastic Leukemia"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"dwhtwh4dj7","title":"Thermal proteome profiling of childhood ALL cell lines for proteoform detection","description":"The complexity of the functional proteome extends significantly beyond the protein coding genome resulting in millions of proteoforms. Investigation of proteoforms and their functional roles is important to understand cellular physiology and its deregulation in diseases, but challenging to perform systematically. Here, we apply thermal proteome profiling with deep peptide coverage to detect functional proteoforms in acute lymphoblastic leukemia cell lines with different cytogenetic aberrations. We detect 15,846 proteoforms, capturing differently spliced, post-translationally modified, and cleaved proteins expressed from 9,290 genes. We identify differential coaggregation of proteoform pairs and establish links to disease biology and drug sensitivity specific biomarkers. This approach provides a powerful and unique tool for systematic detection and functional annotation of proteoform groups.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-26T12:10:47.748Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dwhtwh4dj7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/dwhtwh4dj7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rozbeh","last_name":"Jafari","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nils","last_name":"Kurzawa","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/05072yv34","name":"Barncancerfonden","grant_id":null},{"id":"https://ror.org/056d84691","name":"Karolinska Institutet","grant_id":null},{"id":"https://ror.org/006hbj696","name":"Radium Hemmets Research Funds","grant_id":null},{"id":"https://ror.org/03zttf063","name":"Swedish Research Council","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Mass Spectrometry","Cancer","Proteomics","Acute B-Cell Lymphoblastic Leukemia"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"33tm3dd9dw","title":"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery ","description":"Raw data deposited for \"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery\" by Djamshidi et al-Cell Reports Methods","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-25T15:53:30.358Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/33tm3dd9dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/33tm3dd9dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahbod","last_name":"Djamshidi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Sanger Sequencing","Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":134876,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":146,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":134876,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":134194,"restricted":67,"embargoed":615},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2266},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1330},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":649},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":473},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":439},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":416},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":403},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":381},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":323},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":269}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA"